'''Gummy Cat''' is a [[:Category:Special Cats|Special Cat]] that was added in [[Version 8.5 Update|Version 8.5]] and can be unlocked by purchasing a special sale which contains Gummy Cat and 30 [[Cat Food]]. It was added to promote Japanese Battle Cats gummies. [[True Form]] added in [[Version 11.6 Update|Version 11.6]] increases health and knockbacks while gaining Behemoth Slayer.

{{Cat Info
|ID = 479
|rarity = EX
|name1 = Gummy Cat
|name2 = Lucky Cat
|name3 = Gummy Cat Soda
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Lucky Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Gummy Cat Soda''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit#Behemoth Stones|Behemoth Stones]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
==='''Normal/Evolved Form'''===
Gummy Cat, although having high health compared to most other meatshields, is largely obsolete most of the times in comparison to meatshields such as [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Wall Cat]] or [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Tank Cat]], due to the simple reason of this unit having an excessively high knockback count of 1,000. This means that it won't stay in the frontline for long at all before getting knocked back. This ruins the whole point of Gummy Cat being a meatshield in the first place. Likewise, it has quite a long recharge time compared to most other traditional meatshields, mostly relegating it to [[User Rank]] or early-game encounters. With all this being said, one of its only redeeming factors is its health, but even that is outclassed by a sufficiently leveled Wall Cat or Crazed Tank Cat.

==='''True Form'''===
Gummy Cat Soda unfortunately brings very little to the table in terms of improvements. Even with its HP bonus and a rather high chance to dodge with Behemoth Slayer, Gummy Cat Soda is completely unable to take on the ruthless nature of Behemoth enemies. For this cute little treat, it's either dodge or die. By the time you're able to unlock Gummy Cat's True Form, you should already have much better meatshields at your disposal.

{{Job|Classification = Meatshield & User Rank Dump}}

